WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.772
Validation is not optional. State the row grain.

00:00:03.772 --> 00:00:06.572
Compare totals when the measure is additive.

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:11.577
Check whether NULL values were preserved or filtered intentionally.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:16.152
Inspect the plan for unnecessary scans or shuffles.

00:00:16.152 --> 00:00:21.157
A pipeline is stronger when the result is both correct and explainable.

00:00:21.157 --> 00:00:28.392
Connect this idea to a retail pipeline aggregating high-volume sales data across partitions.

00:00:28.392 --> 00:00:34.447
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:42.837
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.837 --> 00:00:49.132
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:55.340
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
